From c9c659e671368c2bd2b92fdd24ade3b6e44f06e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Langsdorff <131063968+clangsdorff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:02:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] SystemUI: add a media chip to the status bar

show the active media session as an ongoing activity chip, after the
call, screen record and notification chips. the chip uses the app's
small icon, or a music note when that icon is not monochrome, and the
song title in a smaller system font, cut at the width of a chip timer.
a paused session turns the chip tonal with a pause icon. tapping it
opens a compact popup with artwork, title, a seek bar and previous /
play-pause / next. the popup does not expand from the chip, since that
hides the chip while it is open.

the media carousel picks the session, but the title, artwork, play
state and buttons are read from the session callbacks. the carousel
only updates once the app's media notification has gone through the
notification pipeline and its artwork has loaded, which left the chip
behind the app on song changes and play / pause.

status bars that are barely taller than a chip left the chips touching
their top and bottom edges, so cap the chip height to keep a small gap.
